    <bpmn:process id="W_W495" name="W495. ERP Patch, Upgrade &amp; Release Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: ERP vendor release notification; critical security patch; quarterly patch cycle; annual major upgrade
Frequency: Monthly (minor patches); quarterly (cumulative updates); annual (major version upgrade); event-driven (critical security patches)
Volume: ~12 monthly patches; 4 quarterly updates; 1 annual major upgrade; ~2–5 critical security patches/year
Owner: IT — ERP System Administrator
Participants: CIO, IT Manager, Application Support Team, BASIS Team, Key Users (Finance, Supply Chain, HR, Store Ops), IT Security (W367)
Source: workflow W495 — ERP Patch, Upgrade &amp; Release Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W495_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W495_Lane1" name="ERP System Admin">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W495_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W495_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W495_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W495_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W495_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W495_Lane2" name="Application Support Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W495_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W495_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W495_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W495_Lane3" name="IT Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W495_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W495_Lane4" name="CIO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W495_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W495_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W495_Start6" name="ERP vendor release notification; critical security patch; quarterly patch cycle; annual…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W495_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W495_Task7" name="Release Notification &amp; Impact Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Release Notification &amp; Impact Assessment: ERP System Administrator receives vendor release notification: (a) review release notes for: security fixes, functional changes, regulatory updates, deprecated features, integration impacts; (b) assess impact on BuildRight&#x27;s configuration: customizations, integrations (POS, ecommerce, banks, BIR), modified reports, and custom workflows; (c) classify release impact: Critical (security or compliance — apply within SLA), High (affects core processes — apply within 2 weeks), Medium (feature enhancements — apply next quarterly window), Low (cosmetic — defer to next quarterly window); (d) prepare impact assessment report for CIO
Responsible (R): ERP System Admin
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4–8 hours/release</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W495_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W495_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W495_Task8" name="Sandbox Environment Testing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Sandbox Environment Testing: Application Support Team deploys release to sandbox (non-production) environment: (a) deploy to sandbox environment (W384 — ERP environment management); (b) execute regression test suite: POS transaction flow, AP 3-way match (W7), AR billing (W8), payroll processing (W10), inventory transactions (W3/W4), ecommerce integration (W11/W19), bank integration (W30), BIR EIS transmission (W473), intercompany processing (W14); (c) key users from Finance, Supply Chain, HR, and Store Ops perform user acceptance testing (UAT) on critical workflows; (d) document test results and any issues found
Responsible (R): Application Support Team / Key Users
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 3–5 days/release</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W495_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W495_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W495_Task9" name="Customization &amp; Integration Compatibility Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customization &amp; Integration Compatibility Check: Application Support Team verifies: (a) all custom ABAP/SQL code, enhancements, and user exits are compatible with the new release; (b) all integration interfaces (POS, ecommerce, bank, BIR eFPS, EIS, SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG) are compatible; (c) all third-party add-ons and bolt-on solutions are certified for the new release version; (d) all modified reports, forms, and BIR-registered invoice layouts render correctly; (e) if incompatibilities found: work with vendor or internal development (W132) to remediate before production deployment
Responsible (R): Application Support Team
Accountable (A): ERP System Admin
Duration: 2–3 days/release</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W495_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W495_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W495_Task10" name="Go/No-Go Decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Go/No-Go Decision: IT Manager convenes Go/No-Go meeting: (a) review sandbox test results; (b) review customization and integration compatibility status; (c) assess rollback risk; (d) confirm downtime window availability (per NFR-015 batch processing windows); (e) confirm key user availability for post-deployment validation; (f) make Go/No-Go decision; if Go: confirm deployment date and communicate to stakeholders
Responsible (R): IT Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1 hour/meeting</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W495_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W495_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W495_Task11" name="Pre-Deployment Preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Pre-Deployment Preparation: ERP System Administrator prepares for deployment: (a) full system backup (W382); (b) verify rollback plan: how to revert to pre-patch version if critical failure occurs; (c) prepare deployment runbook: step-by-step deployment sequence, verification checkpoints, rollback triggers; (d) notify all stakeholders of planned downtime: Store Managers (POS unavailable), Finance (ERP unavailable), DC Operations (WMS unavailable), ecommerce team (ecommerce maintenance mode); (e) coordinate with POS team for offline POS readiness (W5G) during downtime
Responsible (R): ERP System Admin
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W495_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W495_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W495_Task12" name="Production Deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Production Deployment: ERP System Administrator deploys to production: (a) execute deployment during approved downtime window (typically Saturday night/Sunday morning to minimize impact — per NFR-015); (b) monitor deployment progress; (c) verify deployment at each checkpoint; (d) if deployment fails at any checkpoint: execute rollback per runbook; (e) if deployment succeeds: proceed to post-deployment verification
Responsible (R): ERP System Admin / BASIS Team
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W495_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W495_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W495_Task13" name="Post-Deployment Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-Deployment Verification: Application Support Team and Key Users verify production deployment: (a) smoke test critical workflows: POS transaction, AP invoice posting, AR billing, payroll calculation, inventory movement, BIR EIS transmission; (b) verify all integrations are functioning (POS ↔ ERP, ecommerce ↔ ERP, bank ↔ ERP); (c) verify report generation and dashboard rendering; (d) verify POS terminals are connecting and processing transactions; (e) if issues found: triage severity and apply hotfix or execute rollback; (f) if no issues: confirm deployment success and lift downtime
Responsible (R): Application Support Team / Key Users
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W495_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W495_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W495_Task14" name="Post-Deployment Monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-Deployment Monitoring: ERP System Administrator monitors for 7 days post-deployment: (a) monitor system performance metrics (response time, batch job duration, database load); (b) monitor error logs for new or unusual errors; (c) monitor user-reported issues via helpdesk (W48); (d) if new issues emerge after deployment: assess whether patch-related and apply fix or escalate to vendor; (e) close release in change management log (W132) after 7-day monitoring period
Responsible (R): ERP System Admin
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 7 days monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W495_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W495_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W495_Task15" name="Annual Major Upgrade Planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Annual Major Upgrade Planning: For annual major upgrades (additional steps): (a) start planning 3–6 months before vendor target date; (b) conduct comprehensive impact assessment including all modules, customizations, and integrations; (c) negotiate with vendor for BuildRight-specific upgrade timeline (may differ from standard vendor timeline); (d) plan extended sandbox testing period (4–8 weeks); (e) plan extended downtime window (may require 8–24 hours); (f) plan key user training on new features (W51); (g) plan parallel-run period for critical modules if upgrade includes significant functional changes (W73); (h) budget for upgrade-related consulting or vendor support if needed
Responsible (R): CIO / IT Manager
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 3–6 months planning</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W495_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W495_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W495_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W495_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W495_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-322 (ensure controlled execution — Service Management (PA-27.1).) | - operational: IT — ERP System Administrator review and approval gate
Owner: IT — ERP System Administrator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W495_Assoc18" sourceRef="W495_Annotation17" targetRef="W495_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
