    <bpmn:process id="W_W616" name="W616. ERP Business Change Request &amp; Enhancement Backlog Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Business user submits change request; periodic enhancement cycle
Frequency: Continuous intake; bi-weekly prioritization; monthly release cycle
Volume: ~40–60 change requests/month across all departments
Owner: ERP Application Manager
Participants: Business requestors (all departments), ERP Application Manager, IT Business Analyst, IT Development Lead, Department Heads (prioritization committee)
Source: workflow W616 — ERP Business Change Request &amp; Enhancement Backlog Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W616_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W616_Lane1" name="Business User">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W616_Lane2" name="IT Business Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W616_Lane3" name="Prioritization Committee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W616_Lane4" name="IT Development Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W616_Lane5" name="ERP Application Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W616_End18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W616_Start7" name="Business user submits change request; periodic enhancement cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W616_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W616_Task8" name="Business user submits change request via ERP self-service portal: request type…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Business user submits change request via ERP self-service portal: request type (bug fix, enhancement, new report, workflow modification, integration change), business justification, affected processes, expected benefit, and urgency level (Critical/High/Medium/Low)
Responsible (R): Business User
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W616_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W616_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W616_Task9" name="IT Business Analyst reviews request within 2 business days: validates…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: IT Business Analyst reviews request within 2 business days: validates completeness, clarifies requirements with requestor, assesses technical feasibility, estimates effort (small/medium/large), identifies affected modules and integration points, checks for duplicate or related existing requests
Responsible (R): IT Business Analyst
Accountable (A): ERP Application Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W616_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W616_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W616_Task10" name="IT Business Analyst categorizes request: (a) Configuration change (no code —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: IT Business Analyst categorizes request: (a) Configuration change (no code — user can do via ERP admin tools), (b) Minor enhancement (&lt; 40 hours development), (c) Major enhancement (&gt; 40 hours, requires project charter per W128), (d) Bug/defect, (e) Report/dashboard request
Responsible (R): IT Business Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W616_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W616_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W616_Task11" name="Configuration changes: IT Business Analyst executes directly or guides business…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Configuration changes: IT Business Analyst executes directly or guides business user; tested in sandbox (per W384); moved to production with change management approval (per W132)
Responsible (R): IT Business Analyst
Accountable (A): ERP Application Manager
Duration: 1-4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W616_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W616_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W616_Task12" name="Enhancement requests enter prioritization backlog; IT Business Analyst presents…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Enhancement requests enter prioritization backlog; IT Business Analyst presents new requests to bi-weekly Prioritization Committee (ERP Application Manager, Finance Controller or delegate, Operations representative, IT Development Lead)
Responsible (R): IT Business Analyst
Accountable (A): Prioritization Committee
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W616_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W616_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W616_Task13" name="Prioritization Committee scores each request: (a) Business impact (revenue…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Prioritization Committee scores each request: (a) Business impact (revenue, cost, compliance, user productivity), (b) Number of users/locations affected, (c) Alignment with strategic priorities (per W127), (d) Urgency (compliance deadline, operational risk); weighted score determines backlog ranking
Responsible (R): Prioritization Committee
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W616_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W616_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W616_Task14" name="IT Development Lead assigns approved requests to development sprints (2-week…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: IT Development Lead assigns approved requests to development sprints (2-week sprint cycle); critical bug fixes fast-tracked outside sprint cycle with emergency change process (per W132)
Responsible (R): IT Development Lead
Accountable (A): ERP Application Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W616_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W616_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W616_Task15" name="Development, testing (per W391), and deployment follow software development…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Development, testing (per W391), and deployment follow software development lifecycle (per W132); business user notified of progress and invited to user acceptance testing (UAT)
Responsible (R): IT Development Lead
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Per W132</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W616_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W616_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W616_Task16" name="Post-deployment: IT Business Analyst confirms with requestor that enhancement…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Post-deployment: IT Business Analyst confirms with requestor that enhancement meets requirements; closes change request with satisfaction rating; system logs change history with version tracking
Responsible (R): IT Business Analyst
Accountable (A): Business User
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W616_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W616_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W616_Task17" name="Monthly: ERP Application Manager generates enhancement dashboard — open…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Monthly: ERP Application Manager generates enhancement dashboard — open requests, average resolution time, backlog aging, top requestors, satisfaction scores; presents to CIO and department heads
Responsible (R): ERP Application Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W616_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W616_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W616_End18" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W616_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W616_Annotation19">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-322 (ensure controlled execution — Service Management (PA-27.1).) | - operational: monthly backlog grooming (close stale requests &gt; 6 months old, merge duplicates) and quarterly capacity planning; operational: transparent scoring rubric and committee-based prioritization; operational: scope lock at sprint assignment and change order process for additions
Owner: ERP Application Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W616_Assoc20" sourceRef="W616_Annotation19" targetRef="W616_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W616_Flow21" sourceRef="W616_Start7" targetRef="W616_Task8" />
