    <bpmn:process id="W_W709" name="W709. Enterprise Data Governance &amp; Quality Management Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly data quality review cycle; data quality incident (reporting error, master data duplication, integration failure); new system or data source onboarding; regulatory data requirement
Frequency: Monthly data quality monitoring; quarterly governance council meeting; continuous for incident response
Volume: 35,000 active SKUs, 600,000+ customer records, 800-1,000 vendor records, 200+ location records, 2.8M monthly POS transactions — all requiring data quality assurance
Owner: Data Governance Lead (within IT)
Participants: Data Stewards (per domain: Merchandising for product data, Finance for financial data, HR for employee data, Procurement for vendor data, Operations for location data), IT, Internal Audit, Compliance
Source: workflow W709 — Enterprise Data Governance &amp; Quality Management Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W709_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W709_Lane1" name="Data Governance Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W709_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W709_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W709_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W709_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W709_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W709_Lane2" name="Data Stewards">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W709_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W709_Lane3" name="IT Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W709_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W709_Lane4" name="Internal Audit">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W709_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W709_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W709_Start6" name="Monthly data quality review cycle; data quality incident (reporting error, master data…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W709_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W709_Task7" name="Data governance framework">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Data governance framework: Data Governance Lead maintains enterprise data governance framework: (a) data domains with assigned Data Stewards: Product Master (Merchandising), Customer Master (CRM), Vendor Master (Procurement), Financial Data (Finance), Employee Data (HR), Location Master (Operations), Transactional Data (IT); (b) data quality dimensions measured per domain: Completeness (are all required fields populated?), Accuracy (does data match real-world values?), Timeliness (is data current?), Consistency (is data consistent across systems?), Uniqueness (are there duplicates?); (c) data quality targets per domain (e.g., Item Master completeness ≥ 98%, Customer Master uniqueness ≥ 99%)
Responsible (R): Data Governance Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Initial: 2-3 weeks; ongoing: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W709_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W709_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W709_Task8" name="Monthly data quality monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly data quality monitoring: Data Governance Lead runs automated data quality checks: (a) Item Master: completeness check (required fields: description, UOM, weight, dimensions, category, cost, price), duplicate detection (same description + same barcode), price reasonableness check (selling price &gt; cost price); (b) Customer Master: duplicate detection (same name + same mobile number or email), completeness check (required fields for loyalty, credit, BIR compliance), inactive account cleanup (no transaction in &gt;24 months); (c) Vendor Master: duplicate detection, completeness check (TIN, banking details, contact information), regulatory compliance fields (BIR 2303 currency per W36); (d) Location Master: address accuracy, operating hours, POS terminal mapping; (e) Financial Data: GL account reconciliation anomalies, intercompany imbalance detection per W442
Responsible (R): Data Governance Lead
Accountable (A): Data Stewards
Duration: 4-6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W709_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W709_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W709_Task9" name="Data quality incident response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Data quality incident response: when data quality issue is detected (automated alert or user report): (a) classify severity: Critical (financial impact, customer-facing error, compliance violation), High (operational disruption, reporting inaccuracy), Medium (degraded user experience, workflow inefficiency), Low (cosmetic, non-impactful); (b) Critical/High: Data Governance Lead assigns to Data Steward for immediate remediation with SLA (Critical: 4 hours, High: 24 hours); (c) Medium/Low: Data Steward addresses in next monthly cycle; (d) root cause analysis for Critical incidents: was it a data entry error, integration error, system bug, or process gap?; (e) implement preventive control to avoid recurrence
Responsible (R): Data Governance Lead / Data Stewards
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 15 min (triage) + varies for remediation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W709_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W709_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W709_Task10" name="Master data change impact assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Master data change impact assessment: when significant master data changes are proposed: (a) Item Master: new SKU addition, category reclassification, UOM change — assess impact on open POs, inventory balances, pricing rules, planograms per W86, replenishment parameters per W31; (b) Customer Master: account merge/dedup per W619, credit limit change per W145, tier reclassification per W704 — assess impact on open orders, AR balance, loyalty points; (c) Vendor Master: vendor merge, banking detail change, payment terms change — assess impact on open POs, AP balance, contracted pricing; (d) Data Steward documents impact assessment and routes to affected stakeholders before change is executed
Responsible (R): Data Stewards
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: 30-60 min per assessment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W709_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W709_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W709_Task11" name="Data integration quality monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Data integration quality monitoring: for critical real-time integrations per data-volumes-and-integrations.md: (a) POS to ERP (93,333 transactions/day): monitor transaction completeness (no dropped transactions), price consistency (POS price = ERP price), inventory accuracy (POS deduction = ERP inventory); (b) ERP to Ecommerce (inventory sync every 5 min): monitor sync accuracy (ecommerce stock = ERP stock), price sync accuracy; (c) WMS to ERP (inventory updates &lt;1 min): monitor inventory record consistency; (d) daily reconciliation: compare system counts across integrated systems; (e) alert on integration failures per W595 ERP health check
Responsible (R): IT Operations / Data Governance Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2-3 hours/day (automated monitoring + exception review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W709_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W709_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W709_Task12" name="Quarterly data governance council">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly data governance council: Data Governance Lead convenes quarterly Data Governance Council: (a) attendees: CIO, Data Stewards (all domains), Compliance, Internal Audit; (b) agenda: data quality scorecard (each domain&#x27;s quality metrics vs. targets), Critical/High incident review and trend analysis, upcoming regulatory data requirements (BIR e-invoicing, NPC data privacy), data governance policy updates, data stewardship workload and resource needs; (c) decisions: approve data quality target changes, prioritize data remediation projects, approve new data domains or stewards
Responsible (R): Data Governance Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W709_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W709_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W709_Task13" name="Annual data quality audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual data quality audit: Internal Audit includes data quality in annual audit plan per W359: (a) select sample records from each data domain and verify accuracy against source documents; (b) test data quality controls: duplicate prevention, mandatory field enforcement, approval workflows for changes; (c) test data retention compliance per W256; (d) test data privacy compliance per W647 (customer data access controls, opt-out enforcement); (e) report findings and recommendations to Data Governance Council
Responsible (R): Internal Audit
Accountable (A): Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Duration: 1-2 weeks/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W709_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W709_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W709_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W709_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W709_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-322 (ensure controlled execution — Service Management (PA-27.1).) | - operational: Data Governance Lead (within IT) review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Data Governance Lead (within IT)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W709_Assoc16" sourceRef="W709_Annotation15" targetRef="W709_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
