    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W710" name="W710. Loss Prevention Analytics &amp; Shrinkage Investigation System Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily shrinkage analytics review; exception alert from POS system; periodic inventory count variance per W6; tip-off or whistleblower report; scheduled investigation cycle
Frequency: Daily exception review; weekly analytics reporting; monthly shrinkage analysis; quarterly investigation review
Volume: Shrinkage target: &lt;1.5% of revenue (industry average for hardware retail: 1.5-2.5%); at PHP 62.3B revenue, 1.5% shrinkage = PHP 935M; analytics monitors ~93,000 POS transactions/day + inventory movements + receiving/damage records across 200 stores
Owner: Loss Prevention Manager
Participants: Store Managers (store-level investigations), Regional Managers (regional trend analysis), IT (analytics platform), Internal Audit (investigation support), HR (disciplinary process if needed), Legal (evidence and case management), Security Team
Source: workflow W710 — Loss Prevention Analytics &amp; Shrinkage Investigation System Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W710_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W710_Lane1" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W710_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W710_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W710_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W710_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W710_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W710_Lane2" name="Loss Prevention Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W710_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W710_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W710_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W710_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W710_Start4" name="Daily shrinkage analytics review; exception alert from POS system; periodic inventory…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W710_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W710_Task5" name="Daily exception monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily exception monitoring: LP Analyst reviews automated exception reports from POS and inventory systems: (a) POS void exceptions: high void rates by cashier, voids after large transactions, manager override frequency; (b) refund exceptions: high refund amounts, refund without merchandise return, refunds to same customer frequently; (c) discount exceptions: unauthorized discounts, excessive discount usage, employee discount abuse; (d) inventory exceptions: negative inventory alerts (selling items not in stock per system), receiving quantity variances (PO quantity vs. GR quantity); (e) transaction anomalies: unusually high average transaction value, sweet-hearting patterns (repeated scanning avoidance)
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): Loss Prevention Manager
Duration: 1-2 hours/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W710_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W710_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W710_Task6" name="Weekly shrinkage analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Weekly shrinkage analytics: LP Analyst generates weekly shrinkage analytics report: (a) shrinkage by store: actual shrinkage (from cycle count per W6) vs. target; identify top 20 shrinkage stores; (b) shrinkage by category: which product categories have highest shrinkage (typically power tools, electrical fittings, adhesives — high-value, pocketable items); (c) shrinkage trend: compare to prior week, prior month, same period last year; (d) correlation analysis: shrinkage vs. staffing levels, shrinkage vs. traffic volume, shrinkage vs. LP incident reports; (e) automated alert: stores exceeding shrinkage threshold (&gt;2% of revenue for the period) flagged for investigation
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): Loss Prevention Manager
Duration: 2-3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W710_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W710_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W710_Task7" name="Investigation initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Investigation initiation: when analytics identify suspicious patterns: (a) LP Analyst opens investigation case: case number, store, suspected type (internal theft, external theft, vendor fraud, administrative error), estimated loss amount, supporting data (exception reports, transaction logs, CCTV timestamps); (b) classify investigation: Routine (estimated loss &lt;PHP 50K), Major (PHP 50K-500K), Critical (&gt;PHP 500K or organized pattern); (c) Routine: LP Analyst investigates with Store Manager; Major: Loss Prevention Manager leads investigation with Internal Audit support; Critical: COO + Legal + HR involved
Responsible (R): LP Analyst / Loss Prevention Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 30-60 min per case initiation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W710_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W710_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W710_Task8" name="Evidence gathering">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Evidence gathering: for active investigations: (a) POS transaction log analysis: detailed review of flagged transactions, pattern identification across dates and cashiers; (b) inventory movement audit: trace inventory from receiving per W3 through putaway, sales, and adjustments per W91/W92; (c) CCTV review: for physical stores, review relevant camera footage (retention per W256 — typically 30-90 days); (d) vendor delivery documentation review: verify GR quantities match vendor documentation per W3; (e) digital evidence preservation: screenshots, data exports, and CCTV clips stored per W255 with chain-of-custody documentation for potential legal proceedings
Responsible (R): LP Analyst / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Loss Prevention Manager
Duration: 4-8 hours per investigation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W710_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W710_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W710_Task9" name="Investigation conclusion and action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Investigation conclusion and action: (a) if internal theft confirmed: HR initiates disciplinary process per W152, with Legal review for criminal complaint if warranted; recover losses through salary deduction (per Philippine labor law limits) or civil action; (b) if external theft confirmed: coordinate with local PNP, file criminal complaint with evidence; adjust store security measures per W79; (c) if vendor fraud confirmed: Procurement initiates vendor action per W44/W706 (penalty, de-listing per W36); recover losses through vendor chargeback per W88; (d) if administrative error: implement corrective process and training per W655; (e) all case outcomes documented in LP case management system for trend analysis
Responsible (R): Loss Prevention Manager / HR / Legal
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2-4 hours per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W710_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W710_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W710_Task10" name="Monthly LP analytics reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly LP analytics reporting: Loss Prevention Manager presents monthly report to COO and CFO: (a) total shrinkage: actual vs. target by region, by store, by category; (b) shrinkage as % of revenue trend; (c) investigation case summary: cases opened, closed, by type, by store; (d) recovery: amount recovered through investigations, vendor chargebacks, insurance claims; (e) LP investment ROI: cost of LP operations vs. shrinkage reduction achieved; (f) recommendations: store-level LP improvements, category-specific security measures, policy changes
Responsible (R): Loss Prevention Manager
Accountable (A): COO / CFO
Duration: 4-6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W710_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W710_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W710_Task11" name="Shrinkage reduction program management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Shrinkage reduction program management: Loss Prevention Manager manages ongoing shrinkage reduction initiatives: (a) high-theft category protection: locked display cases for power tools, spider wraps for electronics, EAS tags for high-value items; (b) store layout optimization: camera coverage gaps, blind spots, high-theft category placement near staffed areas; (c) vendor delivery audit program: random receiving audits per W681 for high-shrinkage vendors; (d) employee awareness training: include LP awareness in W51 training curriculum; (e) technology evaluation: evaluate new LP technologies (RFID, AI-powered CCTV analytics, exception-based reporting enhancements) via W691 technology scouting
Responsible (R): Loss Prevention Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Ongoing (~8–12 hours/month)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W710_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W710_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W710_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W710_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W710_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-322 (ensure controlled execution — Service Management (PA-27.1).) | - operational: Loss Prevention Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Loss Prevention Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W710_Assoc14" sourceRef="W710_Annotation13" targetRef="W710_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W710_Flow15" sourceRef="W710_Start4" targetRef="W710_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W710_Flow16" sourceRef="W710_Task5" targetRef="W710_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W710_Flow17" sourceRef="W710_Task6" targetRef="W710_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W710_Flow18" sourceRef="W710_Task7" targetRef="W710_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W710_Flow19" sourceRef="W710_Task8" targetRef="W710_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W710_Flow20" sourceRef="W710_Task9" targetRef="W710_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W710_Flow21" sourceRef="W710_Task10" targetRef="W710_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W710_Flow22" sourceRef="W710_Task11" targetRef="W710_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
