    <bpmn:process id="W_W1409" name="W1409. IT Change Advisory Board (CAB) Weekly Review, Risk Assessment &amp; Deployment Approval" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly CAB meeting cadence (every Wednesday); or emergency CAB for critical production issues
Frequency: Weekly scheduled CAB; emergency CAB as needed (estimated 2–4 per month during peak seasons)
Volume: ~5–15 change requests reviewed per weekly CAB; ~260–780 change requests/year
Owner: IT Change Manager (CIO or designated IT Manager)
Participants: IT Change Manager, IT Infrastructure Lead, Application Support Lead, IT Security Manager, Business Representative (rotating: Store Ops, Finance, Supply Chain, HR), Service Desk Lead
Source: workflow W1409 — IT Change Advisory Board (CAB) Weekly Review, Risk Assessment &amp; Deployment Approval</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1409_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1409_Lane1" name="Change Requestor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1409_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1409_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1409_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1409_Lane2" name="IT Change Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1409_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1409_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1409_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1409_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1409_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1409_Lane3" name="CAB Members">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1409_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1409_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1409_Start5" name="Weekly CAB meeting cadence (every Wednesday); or emergency CAB for critical production…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1409_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1409_Task6" name="Change requestor submits Change Request (CR) in IT Service Management system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Change requestor submits Change Request (CR) in IT Service Management system: (a) description of change, (b) business justification, (c) affected ERP modules and integration points, (d) impacted locations (stores, DCs, HQ), (e) proposed implementation date/time, (f) rollback plan, (g) testing evidence (from test environment per W73), (h) communication plan for affected users; system auto-classifies CR as Standard (pre-approved template), Normal (requires CAB review), or Emergency (expedited approval path)
Responsible (R): Change Requestor (IT staff or business user)
Accountable (A): IT Change Manager
Duration: 30 min/CR</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1409_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1409_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1409_Task7" name="Standard changes">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Standard changes (pre-approved templates: e.g., new user creation per W152, store opening configuration per W16, report parameter changes): IT Change Manager auto-approves without CAB review; change proceeds directly to implementation scheduling
Responsible (R): IT Change Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/CR</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1409_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1409_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1409_Task8" name="Normal changes">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Normal changes: system queues CR for next weekly CAB meeting; IT Change Manager reviews CR for completeness and assigns risk assessment category: (a) Low Risk: cosmetic changes, report formatting, non-critical configuration; (b) Medium Risk: workflow rule changes, new integration endpoints, form modifications; (c) High Risk: ERP module updates, POS system changes, payment integration changes, financial close configuration, database schema changes, security configuration
Responsible (R): IT Change Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min/CR</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1409_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1409_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1409_Task9" name="CAB weekly meeting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: CAB weekly meeting (Wednesday, 60–90 min): IT Change Manager presents all queued normal CRs to CAB members; for each CR: (a) change requestor presents technical details and testing results, (b) Business Representative assesses impact on store operations, financial close, or supply chain, (c) IT Security Manager assesses security impact, (d) CAB discusses implementation timing (prefer Sunday 2:00 AM–6:00 AM maintenance window to avoid POS and store impact), (e) CAB votes: Approve / Approve with Conditions / Reject / Defer for more information
Responsible (R): CAB Members
Accountable (A): IT Change Manager
Duration: 60–90 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1409_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1409_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1409_Task10" name="High-Risk changes">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: High-Risk changes: require additional controls: (a) mandatory weekend maintenance window (Saturday 10 PM – Sunday 6 AM), (b) staging environment deployment and 48-hour soak test before production, (c) pre-deployment communication to all affected Store Managers (via store communication app) 48 hours in advance, (d) IT Infrastructure Lead on standby during and after deployment, (e) automated smoke test of critical functions (POS transaction processing, inventory sync, payment gateway, ecommerce order flow) within 1 hour of deployment, (f) 24-hour monitoring period with hourly health checks
Responsible (R): IT Change Manager / IT Infrastructure Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Additional 2–4 hours/CR</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1409_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1409_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1409_Task11" name="Emergency changes">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Emergency changes (production outage or critical defect): IT Change Manager convenes emergency CAB within 2 hours (virtual meeting or chat channel); minimum 3 CAB members required (IT Change Manager, IT Infrastructure Lead, IT Security Manager); emergency CR approved with conditions: (a) fix deployed immediately, (b) retrospective documentation completed within 24 hours, (c) root cause analysis per W378 within 5 business days, (d) full CAB review of emergency change at next weekly meeting
Responsible (R): IT Change Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–2 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1409_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1409_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1409_Task12" name="Post-implementation: change requestor confirms successful deployment; IT…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-implementation: change requestor confirms successful deployment; IT Service Desk Lead monitors incident queue for 48 hours for any issues related to the change; if issues detected: IT Change Manager initiates rollback per CR rollback plan
Responsible (R): Change Requestor / Service Desk Lead
Accountable (A): IT Change Manager
Duration: 30 min/CR</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1409_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1409_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1409_Task13" name="Monthly: IT Change Manager generates CAB effectiveness report: (a) total CRs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly: IT Change Manager generates CAB effectiveness report: (a) total CRs submitted, approved, rejected, deferred, (b) % of changes implemented on schedule, (c) % of changes causing incidents (change-related incidents), (d) emergency change frequency and root causes, (e) average CR lead time from submission to implementation, (f) CAB meeting attendance rate; report submitted to CIO
Responsible (R): IT Change Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1409_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1409_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1409_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1409_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1409_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-322 (ensure controlled execution — Service Management (PA-27.1).) | - operational: behaves differently after a change
Owner: IT Change Manager (CIO or designated IT Manager)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1409_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1409_Annotation15" targetRef="W1409_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1409_Flow17" sourceRef="W1409_Start5" targetRef="W1409_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1409_Flow18" sourceRef="W1409_Task6" targetRef="W1409_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1409_Flow19" sourceRef="W1409_Task7" targetRef="W1409_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1409_Flow20" sourceRef="W1409_Task8" targetRef="W1409_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1409_Flow21" sourceRef="W1409_Task9" targetRef="W1409_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1409_Flow22" sourceRef="W1409_Task10" targetRef="W1409_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1409_Flow23" sourceRef="W1409_Task11" targetRef="W1409_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1409_Flow24" sourceRef="W1409_Task12" targetRef="W1409_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1409_Flow25" sourceRef="W1409_Task13" targetRef="W1409_End14" />
    </bpmn:process>
