    <bpmn:process id="W_W5521" name="W5521. Enterprise Release Calendar &amp; Peak-Season Change-Freeze Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual peak-calendar planning cycle (ber-months build-up per the W306 seasonal master); upcoming 11.11/12.12 or Warehouse Sale event; freeze-window entry; or an emergency change request during freeze
Frequency: Annual calendar publication; monthly cross-train reconciliation; ~14–16 freeze weeks/year; emergency exceptions as needed
Volume: 3 change engines reconciled — ERP monthly train (W495), built-product weekly rings (W5517), infrastructure/store patches (W367); ~600+ change events/year; ~30 freeze exceptions/year
Owner: IT Change Manager (CIO or designated IT Manager)
Participants: Application Manager, Head of Engineering, IT Security Manager, IT Infrastructure Manager, VP Store Operations, VP Supply Chain, Service Desk Lead, Regional Managers
Source: workflow W5521 — Enterprise Release Calendar &amp; Peak-Season Change-Freeze Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5521_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5521_Lane1" name="IT Change Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5521_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5521_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5521_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5521_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5521_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5521_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5521_Lane2" name="App Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5521_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5521_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5521_Start4" name="Annual peak-calendar planning cycle (ber-months build-up per the W306 seasonal master)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5521_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5521_Task5" name="Annual freeze-calendar publication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual freeze-calendar publication: Map freeze windows onto the merchandising peak calendar (ber-months build-up, 11.11/12.12, payday weekends, Warehouse Sale, Holy Week) using the seasonal master (W306); publish to all change engines
Responsible (R): IT Change Mgr
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 24 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5521_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5521_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5521_Task6" name="Monthly cross-train reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly cross-train reconciliation: Align the ERP monthly train (W495), the built-product ring dashboard (W5517) and infrastructure/store patch cycles (W367) onto the single release calendar; resolve collisions
Responsible (R): IT Change Mgr / App Manager
Accountable (A): IT Change Mgr
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5521_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5521_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5521_Task7" name="Freeze-entry readiness gate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Freeze-entry readiness gate: Per window — Tier-1 system health (W595), support staffing &amp; hypercare rota (VS-134), rollback plans on file, freeze communications to stores/regional teams (VS-63)
Responsible (R): IT Change Mgr / Service Desk Lead
Accountable (A): IT Change Mgr
Duration: 4 hours/week during freeze</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5521_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5521_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5521_Task8" name="Exception adjudication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Exception adjudication: Business-critical/emergency changes during freeze via CAB risk assessment (W1409) with Store Operations sign-off for store-facing changes; log and report exceptions
Responsible (R): IT Change Mgr / CAB
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1 hour/exception × ~30/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5521_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5521_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5521_Task9" name="Freeze-exit &amp; backlog flush">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Freeze-exit &amp; backlog flush: Sequence the deferred backlog post-peak; stagger high-risk releases to avoid a risky batch landing
Responsible (R): App Manager / IT Change Mgr
Accountable (A): IT Change Mgr
Duration: 8 hours/peak × 2</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5521_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5521_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5521_Task10" name="Post-peak review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-peak review: Incident/change-failure review feeding W378 problem management and next-year calendar adjustments
Responsible (R): IT Change Mgr / Service Desk Lead
Accountable (A): IT Change Mgr
Duration: 8 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5521_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5521_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5521_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5521_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5521_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-322 (ensure controlled execution — Service Management (PA-27.1).) | - operational: freeze exceptions require CAB risk assessment (W1409) with Store Operations sign-off | - operational: the release calendar is CIO-approved before publication
Owner: IT Change Manager (CIO or designated IT Manager)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
